[ ] formatter serialization bug emits adjacent fields without whitespace separating them !1 +bug #019e6da7-9c35-7852-9b87-6e69af96be65
[ ] grammar rejects malformed UUIDs as syntax errors instead of letting the linter flag them $ E006_invalid_uuid inputs like #123 or #abc-def parse to syntax-error + missing-id, so the E006 invalid-uuid lint rule never fires — tests/linting_conformance.rs test_linting_error_detection has been red on main since 6861516 ("linting more hardcore") tightened the id grammar. this is a Decision 6 violation: the tree-sitter grammar should accept a malformed #id permissively and let the E006 linter catch the bad format, not error the whole line. worse, a syntax-error can drop the action from loads entirely — the same silent-dropout class the [[trust]] doctor fsck targets. fix in tree-sitter-actions (permissive id token) so the id parses instead of erroring — same grammar-too-strict class as the [[trust]] reserved-char escaping work. NOTE the lint side is now two jobs, not one: the existing E006 catches truly invalid formats, but a NEW linting rule is needed to capture INCOMPLETE uuids — partial hyphenated forms like 01950000-0000-7000-8000 or 12345678-1234 that a valid short-prefix check (8+ contiguous hex) would otherwise wave through. incomplete-while-typing is the live-buffer case (Decision 6), so it lint-warns, never errors $ !2 +bug,library #019f2abc-af8d-76c4-a1a5-65e9c7ffcc12
